v2 changelog
============

Running log of every change made toward v2 (the soldier-swarm
rebuild). One entry per change. WHAT + WHY, kept short.

Plan of record: port.md
Lessons from v1:    lessons.md

When v2 moves to its own repo, this file moves with it as the
seed of that repo's CHANGELOG / dev_log.

---

2026-05-09  Commit A verified live on phone (both URLs)
  WHAT: User opened both URLs on phone after Pages rebuild:
        v1 → /Territorygame/    → loads (existing game intact).
        v2 → /Territorygame/swarm/ → loads (scaffold "ok" text).
        Both confirmed working. port.md updated with the locked
        stack/deploy section and a Nail-1 spec section so future
        Claude doesn't re-derive these decisions.
  WHY:  Mantra checkpoint. Per "nail one aspect before the next,"
        commit A (the scaffold + Pages plumbing) is officially
        nailed: works on phone, no TODOs, logged. Cleared to
        start commit B (camera + grid + crossfade + input).

---

2026-05-09  Commit A: swarm/ scaffold builds + deploys to /docs/swarm/
  WHAT: Standalone vite + TS + Pixi 8 + zustand project under
        swarm/. Builds to ../docs/swarm with base
        /Territorygame/swarm/, so GH Pages serves v2 at
        /Territorygame/swarm/ alongside v1 at /Territorygame/.
        main.ts is the minimum: boot Pixi, full-window canvas,
        write "scaffold ok" to a debug readout. No game state,
        no input, no zoom yet. Sourcemaps off, no lint/test
        scaffolding (lean per user's "don't inflate" note).
        Deps: pixi.js ^8.6, zustand ^5. That's it.
  WHY:  Per the mantra, ship the scaffold as its own discrete
        step before the actual nail. Verifies the
        build → docs/swarm/ → Pages pipeline so when commit B
        adds the zoom, any breakage points at the feature, not
        the plumbing. Bundle: ~140 KB gzipped (pixi auto-chunked
        into webgl/gpu/canvas paths).

